/-! # Ordered nodal branches on an étale overlap

Source: agent reconstruction of the branch-comparison argument after Stacks Project,
curves.tex, Tag 0CBY, lemma-etale-local-structure-nodal-family. That tag supplies the
initial charts; the finite-height ordering argument is additional
(blueprint: lem-trf-ordered-nodal-branch-overlap).
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The coordinate `u` (`i = 0`) or `v` (`i = 1`) on `Spec A[u,v]/(uv-c)`.
This uses the existing standard nodal algebra, without choosing any generators.
Source: Stacks Project, curves.tex, Tag 0CBY, universal nodal chart
(blueprint: lem-trf-ordered-nodal-branch-overlap). -/
def strictNodalCoordinate (A : CommRingCat.{u}) (c : A) (i : Fin 2) :
    Γ((StrictSemistableModel.nodal c).scheme, ⊤) :=
  (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of (strictNodalRing A c))).inv
    (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPolynomial.X i))

/-- The principal ideal generated by the germ of a pulled-back nodal coordinate,
in the local ring of the total source scheme (before passage to a fibre).
Source: the branch-comparison argument after Stacks Project, curves.tex, Tag 0CBY
(blueprint: lem-trf-ordered-nodal-branch-overlap). -/
def strictNodalCoordinateIdeal {A : CommRingCat.{u}} (c : A) {T : Scheme.{u}}
    (q : T ⟶ (StrictSemistableModel.nodal c).scheme) (z : T) (i : Fin 2) :
    Ideal (T.presheaf.stalk z) :=
  Ideal.span {(T.presheaf.germ ⊤ z trivial) (q.appTop (strictNodalCoordinate A c i))}

/-- After shrinking a pointed étale nodal chart, its two labelled coordinate ideals
agree at every fibre-component generic point of its self-overlap. No descent of
these ideals, or Zariski-local étale nodal chart on the target, is asserted.

Source: agent reconstruction after Stacks Project, curves.tex, Tag 0CBY,
lemma-etale-local-structure-nodal-family; Temkin §4.3, printed p. 27 is motivation only
(blueprint: lem-trf-ordered-nodal-branch-overlap).

Proof plan, in the order of the DAG node:
1. Shrink the finite-chain valuation base to the generizations of the image of y.
   This is a principal affine open and its ring is the corresponding localization.
   Étale base change and restriction preserve the two charts; affine étale maps
   are finitely presented (etale-base-change-finite-limits,
   etale-composition-cancellation, qcqs-morphism-permanence).
2. For every prime t containing c, the closed branch schemes V(t,u) and V(t,v)
   are étale over the polynomial lines over V/t. This quotient is a valuation
   domain. Valuation-ring-normal, polynomial-ring-normal-domain,
   localization-normal-domain and etale-over-normal-ring-normal show the branches
   are normal.
3. Their spaces are Noetherian: each of the finitely many fibres is finite type
   over a field (finite-type-over-noetherian, affine-noetherian-underlying-space).
   Normal-topologically-noetherian-components separates their finitely many
   integral clopen components. Remove all components not containing y and take
   an affine neighbourhood Y1 of y. Do this for both labels and every t.
4. V(u,v) in Y1 is étale over the local spectrum V/(c); its open image contains
   the closed point, so meets every fibre containing c (flat-lfp-open).
5. Each retained integral branch is flat over V/t. Its coordinate ring contains
   V/t injectively, so generic-fibre-localization-domain-irreducible makes its
   fibre over t integral; step 4 makes it nonempty. Flat-ring-map and its affine
   comparison justify the flatness assertions.
6. The two branches cover that fibre and neither contains the other, since each
   maps openly to its affine line and meets its origin. The fibre is reduced by
   etale-proposition-etale-reduced. The origin is nonsmooth: u,v mapping to epsilon
   over k[epsilon]/(epsilon^2) cannot lift over k[epsilon]/(epsilon^3).
   Etale-source-smoothness reflects this obstruction through the chart.
7. An open map between these Noetherian fibres sends a component generic point
   to a component generic point: remove the other finitely many source components
   and use openness. Use noetherian-finite-irreducible-components and flat-lfp-open.
8. The two image components are distinct. Otherwise the fibre map factors through
   their common reduced component, which is smooth by hypothesis. Vanishing on
   both branches implies vanishing on the fibre, by flat-tensor-exact applied to
   k[u,v]/(uv) into k[u] plus k[v]. The factor is étale by base change, hence the
   fibre would be smooth by etale-smooth-zero-dimensional-fibres and smooth-ring-map
   affine comparison and composition, contradicting step 6.
9. Choose a principal affine neighbourhood U of p(y) inside p(Y1); its inverse
   image Y0 in Y1 is affine, contains y, and maps surjectively to U. The retained
   branch and distinct-image properties persist under this restriction.
10. Both projections of W = Y0 ×_U Y0 are étale and open. Its fibres have finitely
    many components by finite-type-over-noetherian, affine-noetherian-underlying-space
    and noetherian-finite-irreducible-components. Their component generic points
    project to generic points on the same labelled branch, since the two images
    in U coincide. Thus both u coordinates, or both v coordinates, are units
    at such a point. If c is a unit all four coordinates are units. Fibres outside
    the retained base open are empty.
11. In the total local ring at this point, uv=c. When both v coordinates are
    units, the u ideals are both (c) and the v ideals both (1); interchange u,v
    in the other case. These give precisely the two asserted ideal equalities.
-/
theorem exists_ordered_nodal_branch_overlap
    (K : Type u) [Field K] [IsSepClosed K] (V : ValuationSubring K)
    [Finite (PrimeSpectrum V)] {X Y : Scheme.{u}} [IsAffine X] [IsAffine Y]
    (f : X ⟶ Spec (.of V)) [Flat f] [LocallyOfFinitePresentation f]
    (hfib : ∀ (Ω : Type u) [Field Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω]
      (g : Spec (.of Ω) ⟶ Spec (.of V)),
      (pullback (C := Scheme.{u}) f g).IsPureDimension 1 ∧
        ∀ z : pullback (C := Scheme.{u}) f g, z ∉ (pullback.snd (C := Scheme.{u}) f g).smoothLocus →
          Nonempty
            (AdicCompletion
                (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ((pullback (C := Scheme.{u}) f g).presheaf.stalk z))
                ((pullback (C := Scheme.{u}) f g).presheaf.stalk z) ≃+*
              (MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) Ω ⧸
                Ideal.span {(MvPowerSeries.X 0 : MvPowerSeries (Fin 2) Ω) *
                  MvPowerSeries.X 1})))
    (hcomponents : ∀ (s : Spec (.of V)) (Z : TopologicalSpace.Closeds (f.fiber s)),
      (Z : Set (f.fiber s)) ∈ irreducibleComponents (f.fiber s) →
        Smooth ((Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal Z).subschemeι ≫
          f.fiberToSpecResidueField s))
    (c : V) (hc : c ≠ 0) (p : Y ⟶ X) [Etale p]
    (h : Y ⟶ (StrictSemistableModel.nodal (A := .of V) c).scheme) [Etale h]
    (hover : h ≫ (StrictSemistableModel.nodal (A := .of V) c).baseMap = p ≫ f)
    (y : Y) (hy : p y ∉ f.smoothLocus)
    (horigin : ∀ i : Fin 2,
      Y.evaluation ⊤ y trivial (h.appTop (strictNodalCoordinate (.of V) c i)) = 0) :
    ∃ (U : X.Opens) (Y0 : Y.Opens) (_ : IsAffineOpen U) (_ : IsAffineOpen Y0)
      (e : Y0 ≤ p ⁻¹ᵁ U),
      p y ∈ U ∧ y ∈ Y0 ∧ Surjective (p.resLE U Y0 e) ∧
        ∀ (s : Spec (.of V))
          (ξ : (pullback.fst (C := Scheme.{u}) (p.resLE U Y0 e) (p.resLE U Y0 e)
              ≫ Y0.ι ≫ p ≫ f).fiber s)
          (Z : Set
            ((pullback.fst (C := Scheme.{u}) (p.resLE U Y0 e) (p.resLE U Y0 e)
                ≫ Y0.ι ≫ p ≫ f).fiber s)),
          Z ∈ irreducibleComponents
            ((pullback.fst (C := Scheme.{u}) (p.resLE U Y0 e) (p.resLE U Y0 e)
                ≫ Y0.ι ≫ p ≫ f).fiber s) →
          IsGenericPoint ξ Z → ∀ i : Fin 2,
            strictNodalCoordinateIdeal (A := .of V) c
                (pullback.fst (C := Scheme.{u}) (p.resLE U Y0 e) (p.resLE U Y0 e) ≫ Y0.ι ≫ h)
                ((pullback.fst (C := Scheme.{u}) (p.resLE U Y0 e) (p.resLE U Y0 e)
                    ≫ Y0.ι ≫ p ≫ f).fiberι s ξ) i =
              strictNodalCoordinateIdeal (A := .of V) c
                (pullback.snd (C := Scheme.{u}) (p.resLE U Y0 e) (p.resLE U Y0 e) ≫ Y0.ι ≫ h)
                ((pullback.fst (C := Scheme.{u}) (p.resLE U Y0 e) (p.resLE U Y0 e)
                    ≫ Y0.ι ≫ p ≫ f).fiberι s ξ) i := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
